  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G5P">Example <span data-tag="0G5P">14.33.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$, $Y$, $d$, $s$ be as in Example <a href="/tag/0G5M" data-tag="0G5M">14.33.1</a> satisfying the equations of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G5N" data-tag="0G5N">14.33.2</a>. Given functors $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{C}$ and $G : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{B}$ we obtain a simplicial object $G \circ X \circ F$ in the category of functors from $\mathcal{A}$ to $\mathcal{B}$ which comes with an augmentation to $G \circ F$. </p>
